 have betrayed the  location of the podoglyph and pluton to  the world government so the nefertari  had to remain in alabasta and they had  to pretend to support the world  government while secretly preparing for  joy boy's return this secret mission  that the nefertari family had taken upon  themselves may have been forgotten over  the many centuries and as such it is  possible that king cobra and vivi don't  even know the truth at the moment but i  believe that they will be made aware of  it when the time is right or rather vivi  will because king cobra may already be  dead after the reverie that being said i  do believe that vv will eventually learn  the truth about joyboy's plan and the  ancient weapon pluton and all of this  will play an important role in the final  showdown of the series  so here's what we know about joyboy's  master plan so far in order to set the  stage for his eventual return the kozuki  clan created the ponoglyphs and made a  pact with the minks the nefertari family  infiltrated the world government from  within and the joy boy's eventual return  was foretold both on the ryugyu  ponoglyph and on laughtale there are  still several other components to  joyboy's plan including the d-clan the  straw hat and even the famous c-shanty  binks sake and yeah i know that some of  you might think i'm crazy for claiming  that an innocent pirate song like bing  sake is part of some secret master plan  so let's address that first pink sake is  a famous sea shanty that has been sung  by pirates for centuries and in fact i  am proposing that it has been around  ever since the void century being sake  is not just a song it is actually an  oral history which tells the tragic  story of the void century the dawn of  the world and laugh tale i mean the  final line of the song actually contains  the term varayi banashi which can be  literally translated as laugh tale never  ending never wandering our funny  traveling tale are laugh tale the entire  song is full of potentially important  clues going to deliver being sake by  sailing to the ends of the sea i.e to  the final island if you lose your nerve  this breath could be your last but if  you just hold on the morning sun will  rise the dawn of the world the sun god  nika i mean you get the point a lot can  be read into these lyrics and with good  reason what better way to preserve an  important message for future generations  in a world where the truth has been  banned and erased from history than to  preserve it as something like a song or  poem something that never needs to be  written down and yet can be passed on  from generation to generation a funny  tale that keeps traveling from one  generation to the next in fact i have  some personal experience with this kind  of thing i am serbian and epic poems  that were passed down orally from  generation to generation played an  important role in our history the  serbian people lived under occupation by  the ottoman empire for centuries and any  books or other written records that  celebrated serbian heroes who fought  against the ottomans would have been  prohibited on top of that most people  were illiterate anyway so even if  written records did exist no one would  have been able to read them so the  serbian people passed on their history  in the form of epic poems which told the  stories of medieval serbian heroes who  fought against the ottomans and also  stories of the haiduk's serbian outlaws  who waged the guerrilla-style war  against the ottoman occupiers for  centuries these epic poems were passed  on from generation to generation orally  so each new poet had to memorize the  entire poem in order to share it with  others it was only in the 1800s that  these poems were actually written down  and published as part of various  collections so yeah if joyboy wanted to  send a secret message to future  generations a message which gave them  hints about laugh tale and the dawn of  the world pink's sake would have been  the perfect method in fact the lyrics of  being sake may turn out to be even more  important than we thought because they  could be a part of a cipher that will  eventually be used to unlock an  important secret such as the location of  the ancient weapons or something along  those lines and this brings me to the  true meaning of the straw hat including  that mysterious giant straw hat in  marijua  there are several loose threads that we  need to pick up and bring together in  order to discover the real meaning  behind the straw hat first up we have  the lyrics of being sake once again one  thing that caught my eye early on was  the fact that the viz and funimation  versions of the translation include the  phrase bid farewell to weaver's town as  in a town where something is being  weaved in other versions this is  translated as hometown but both versions  work for what i am about to say next if  we go back to chapter 272  we see that on the ruins of shandora  there is a text written in the same  ancient script that was used on the  poneglyphs these are the words that  robin reads there hold the truth in your  heart keep your mouth silent we are the  ones who weave history with the  reverberations of the great bell this  short text implies that a secret is  preserved in your heart but kept hidden  from the outside world it also implies  that this secret is deeply tied to  history to important historical events  and whoever wrote the text clearly  intends to influence history to weave  history in some way finally there's  toki's prophecy from chapter 919  right before she apparently died toki  proclaimed like the moon you are  ignorant of the dawn if there is one  ardent wish that must be fulfilled it  will be when nine shadows are cast woven  together through 20 years of moonlit  nights only then shall you understand  the radiance of dawn these different  bits of information may not seem  connected at first and they are hundreds  of chapters apart in the manga but they  do have a common thread and yes pun  intended because i'm talking about the  reference to weaving bidding farewell to  weaver's town we are the ones who weave  history shadows woven together through  20 years and how is a straw hat created  in the first place  through the process of weaving the  weaver's town or hometown in bing sake  is the ancient kingdom bing sake which  they are delivering is the secret  history that joy boy and his followers  are protecting and it is also the ideal  of freedom that they want to bring out  of the void century and into the present  time the void century is a part of  history that was erased by the world  government a part of history that was  ripped from the fabric of time but  joyboy and his followers are keeping the  threads alive so that one day this  important piece of history that was  ripped out can be woven back together  again and once it is woven back together  once the truth comes out the world  government will fall because the message  of freedom and equality that the ancient  kingdom represents is too powerful for  the tyranny of the world government to  overcome that is exactly why they went  through all that trouble to erase it  from history because they know how  dangerous to their very existence this  idea is the straw hat is woven together  from straw just like the dawn of the  world will one day be woven together  from all the secret and seemingly loose  threads that joyboy and the ancient  kingdom left behind the straw hat is the  most simple and most visible enduring  symbol of the dawn of the world and its  passing from generation to generation  mirrors the passing of bink's sake from  generation to generation it also mirrors  the passing of the information hidden on  the pondoglyphs from generation to  generation and so on the world  government loathes the straw hat because  it symbolizes everything they fear the  most and everything that they try to  erase from history on the surface the  straw hat may seem like a completely  innocent and innocuous accessory but for  those who know and are trying to hide  the truth about the void century the  straw hat is nothing less than a  declaration of war and all of this talk  about weaving threads of fate brings me  to another important topic the fates in  greek mythology we already know that oda  takes a lot of inspiration from greek  mythology after all all three ancient  weapons are based on deities from greek  mythology and yes this includes pluton  pluton is often associated with roman  mythology but the romans got the word  and the deity from the greeks now in  greek mythology the fates are three  women who determine the destiny of  everything and everyone and on many  occasions they are said to have even  greater power than the gods they spend  their entire days spinning the threads  of fate their thread is the line of life  itself and once a thread is snipped off  the person whose lifeline that was dies  clotho is the woman who spins a new  thread when a new baby is born la cases  determines the length of each thread and  atropos chooses the cause of death for  each person and she then snips the  thread when that person's life is  supposed to end since they are the ones  who decide destiny the ones who weave  destiny the fates know what will happen  in the future and all oracles and  prophecies are just tiny glimpses into  what the fates know i think that this  concept of the fates will become more  important in one piece as the story  continues and all of those prophecies  about the dawn of the world and the  concept of the will of thee will one day  be woven together like the threads of  fate or the threads of a straw hat we  may even see the three fates from greek  mythology being associated with the  three ancient weapons uranus could be  the nika devil fruit which has been  reincarnated inside a new person a new  thread poseidon controls powerful living  creatures the seekings which symbolizes  life and the threat of life itself and  of course pluton is a battleship which  can destroy life and so it snips the  threads of many now let's circle back to  the straw hat and especially that giant  straw hat that is being held inside a  freezing vault-like room in marijuana  this i admit is a real mystery and many  have suggested that this could be the  straw hat that belonged to the original  joy boy however if the world government  is trying to completely erase joy boy  the ancient kingdom and their symbols  from history then why would they not  destroy the straw hat  why keep it in this strange room as if  trying to preserve it when you could  just destroy it and then no one would  ever find it while i believe that the  straw hat in general is a symbol of joy  boy's master plan and therefore of joy  boy's will could this specific hat have  some sort of special ability which makes  it impossible to destroy and is the cold  temperature required in order to keep  this hat's special power from activating  potentially but the hat could also be  one of the keys to deciphering the truth  about joyboy's master plan maybe imusama  is keeping it on ice because it actually  contains some important information like  maybe something is written on it or  engraved inside of it and maybe the cold  is somehow preventing the letters from  fading or something i don't know i'm not  a scientist perhaps imusama knows that  there's a secret message on the straw  hat but he or she is unable to decipher  it at this point for some reason but  this message might be too important to  destroy and so the hat has been  preserved it's hard to say what's really  going on with this straw hat based on  the limited information that we have so  far but there has to be some good reason  why this hat has been carefully  preserved rather than just destroyed  along with everything else related to  the ancient kingdom i could totally see  robin finally solving the mystery of the  giant straw hat during the climax of the  story but we'll have to wait and see  definitely let me know what you think of  the giant straw hat at marijuana what is  its significance and why hasn't it been  destroyed why is it being kept in this  frozen vault almost like imusama is  deliberately trying to preserve it let  me know down below finally we need to  talk about the d clan because along with  the ponoglyphs the nefertari family bing  sake and the straw hat i believe that  the d-clan is also an important aspect  of joy boy's master plan  there are a ton of theories out there on  what the d-clan is and what the d stands  for in a previous video i argued that  perhaps only members of the d-clan are  able to awaken the nika devil fruit and  because the d-clan members are so rare  no one was able to awaken the fruit  until luffy but even if that were the  case it still wouldn't explain where the  d-clan actually came from what makes  them so special some have suggested that  members of the d-clan are all  descendants of the original joy boy  meaning that they are all related by  blood but because it's been 800 years  since the death of joy boy they are very  distant relatives and over the centuries  many of them forgot what the d in their  name even means this theory would have  to account for the fact that giants like  jaguar d saul and his family are also  members of the d-clan but if we assume  that giants and humans can't have  children with each other then this  theory could technically be possible  another popular theory is that the  d-clan are descendants of the original  joy boys crew so they're not all related  by blood but they do all trace their  origins to the void century and to  joyboy himself i think that this second  scenario is more likely i believe that  joyboy created the d-clan himself in  order to advance his master plan a plan  that would only come to fruition  centuries after his death members of the  d clan may be descendants of joy boy's  crew or they may be the descendants of a  secret society that joyboy established a  secret society dedicated to advancing  his master plan and his will after his  death either way it's clear to me that  members of the d-clan have an important  role to play in the coming final  showdown against the world government  and they will almost certainly turn out  to be instrumental in ushering in the  dawn of the world now several big  questions remain do the members of the  d-clan have any sort of special powers  or abilities compared to normal people  are they more likely to embrace the will  of joy boy than normal people and if so  why and what does the d stand for anyway  the d could stand for destiny because  they are destined to fulfill joyboy's  plan or for devil in the sense that  devils are the enemies of gods and the  d-clan are the natural enemies of the  celestial dragons but i think that the d  very likely stands for dawn because that  word dawn is everywhere in one piece and  it has been foreshadowed from the very  beginning romance dawn is the name of  the very first chapter the dawn of the  world is the epic world changing event  that the kozuki and the minks have been  waiting for for centuries toki's  prophecy places a strong emphasis on the  coming dawn and so on members of the  d-clan may have a special will that has  somehow been inherited by each and every  one of them the will of joyboy which  will one day fulfill joyboy's master  plan and bring about the dawn of the  world but if that is the case we would  need some sort of explanation for how  this will is inherited in the first  place we know that devil fruits seem to  have a will of their own but it appears  that not all members of the d-clan have  been devil fruit users  goldie roger was not a devil fruit user  as kaido confirmed in chapter 1047  and this means that roger could not have  inherited any sort of will from a devil  fruit so if the connection isn't devil  fruits what is the explanation do  members of the d-clan just have some  sort of special destiny are they all  chosen ones who are favored by the gods  or the universe or something or are they  just normal people who happen to find  themselves in extraordinary situations  because that de-initial in their names  leads others to treat them differently  which makes it all a sort of  self-fulfilling prophecy i think it's  probably a little bit of both  members of the d-clan do have a special  role to play in the one-piece story  which means that fate is definitely a  factor here but i would like to argue  that it's not just about fate throughout  the course of this video i've been  suggesting that the original joyboy  predicted his own defeat and death and  that he carefully constructed a master  plan that has been 800 years in the  making this plan involved the kozuki  clan and the ponoglyphs the alliance  between the kozuki and the minx in  anticipation of the dawn of the world  the nefertari family's refusal to live  in marijua the treasure left behind on  laughtale the true meaning of being sake  and the powerful symbolism of the straw  hat the existence of the d clan is  likely another aspect of joyboy's plan  it wasn't fate that formed the d-clan in  the first place it was joyboy himself  we don't know what exactly makes the  d-clan special we don't know whether  they possess a special power or a  special destiny but i believe that their  origins can be traced directly back to  joy boy and the secret master plan that  he set into motion over 800 years ago  maybe the d-clan are descendants of  joyboy's crew or maybe they're the  descendants of a secret society that was  formed after the fall of the ancient  kingdom in order to keep joyboy's ideals  alive in secret  whatever their true origins are i don't  think that their existence will turn out  to be a coincidence or an act of fate  they are not individuals who were chosen  by gods or by the universe instead they  were deliberately chosen by joy boy as  part of a wide-ranging master plan for  finally defeating the world government  and ushering in the dawn of the world we  still don't know all the specific  details of this master plan we only have  a rough outline that includes many loose  threads  but these threads will be woven together  eventually just like the threads in a  straw hat in order to reveal the epic  climax of the entire one piece story  if you guys enjoyed this video and you  want to see more in the future leave a  quick like and comment it only takes a  second but it helps me with that youtube  algorithm and remember that subscribing  and hitting that notification bell is a  completely free but very real way of  directly supporting the channel don't  forget to let me know what you think the  d clan is down in the comments below i  really want to hear your takes finally  if you're looking for a video to watch  next check out my video on the void  century link in the description as  always thank you guys so much for  watching and until next time see ya  space cowboys
 

